PMID- 42550655
OWN - NLM
STAT- MEDLINE
DCOM- 20260804
LR  - 20260804
IS  - 2694-3611 (Electronic)
IS  - 2694-3581 (Linking)
VI  - 108
IP  - 1
DP  - 2026
TI  - From Bedside to Blueprint: The Role of the Public Health Nurse in Strategic 
      Military Health Facility Planning.
PG  - 139-141
AB  - Public health nurses are often associated with disease prevention and 
      community-based health education. Yet their contributions extend far beyond 
      clinical and community interactions. In the context of military healthcare, 
      public health nurses bring a systems-oriented perspective that supports 
      long-range strategic planning, readiness, and resilience. This article offers a 
      firsthand account of how nursing experience, rooted in frontline outbreak 
      response and humanitarian missions, evolved into strategic leadership within the 
      U.S. Army Health Facility Planning Agency (HFPA). HFPA is charged with designing 
      and modernizing healthcare delivery systems across the Department of Defense, 
      integrating clinical operations with infrastructure planning to support military 
      operations worldwide. Public health nurses are uniquely qualified to contribute 
      to this mission. Their training in prevention, population health, epidemiology, 
      and health equity informs facility design that not only meets immediate clinical 
      needs but anticipates long-term shifts in disease burden, demographic changes, 
      and emerging health threats. This article explores the intersection of public 
      health nursing, strategic planning, and military health systems through the 
      example of a hospital redevelopment project in Chuuk State, Federated States of 
      Micronesia. It underscores how public health insights can strengthen healthcare 
      access and reinforce global health partnerships that align with operational 
      readiness. By embedding nursing expertise into the fabric of infrastructure 
      design, the future of military healthcare can be proactive and responsive.
