TI  - 8S From Efficiency To Innovation: The Evolution And Future Of The Nurse Methods 
      Analyst In Army Medicine.
PG  - 80-81
AB  - The Army Nurse Corps' Nurse Methods Analyst (NMA) role has evolved significantly 
      since its post-World War II origins focused on hospital efficiency. Today, NMAs 
      are critical to optimizing patient care and operational readiness through data 
      analysis, systems design, and health informatics. This article traces the 
      historical development of the NMA, from initial staffing standardizations to 
      foundational work in patient categorization systems that preceded modern workload 
      management tools. It highlights the NMA's current and future role in supporting a 
      leaner, more lethal force, particularly through leveraging artificial 
      intelligence and strategic partnerships to address evolving healthcare demands 
      within both fixed facilities and operational environments. The NMA community is 
      poised to lead innovation in clinical operations, manpower management, and the 
      integration of technology to maintain military superiority.
