TI  - Active-Duty Sailor Develops PFO-Associated Decompression Sickness: Do 
      Occupational Divers Warrant Alternative Cardiac Screening Standards?
PG  - 678-682
LID - S0735-1097(24)07576-4 [pii]
LID - 10.1016/j.jacc.2024.06.010 [doi]
AB  - We report a case of an active-duty diver who developed severe decompression 
      sickness with concomitant patent foramen ovale that was successfully closed 
      contrary to standard guideline recommendations. This case should prompt 
      evaluation of the role of cardiac screening in occupational divers, including 
      tactical athletes, relative to recreational divers.
