TI  - Congenital Long QT Syndrome and Cardiac Arrest in a Military Tactical Athlete.
PG  - 101990
LID - 10.1016/j.jaccas.2023.101990 [doi]
LID - 101990
AB  - We present a case of a U.S. marine who experienced cardiac arrest during military 
      Special Forces underwater diving exercises whose evaluation revealed congenital 
      long QT syndrome. This case highlights the expanding role for systematic 
      electrocardiogram screening in target athletic and military populations given 
      their stress and tactical exposures. (Level of Difficulty: Advanced.).
