TI  - Military crisis responses to COVID-19.
PG  - 99-103
LID - 10.1111/1468-5973.12328 [doi]
AB  - Countries across the globe have mobilized their armed forces in response to the 
      COVID-19 pandemic. Current contributions of armed forces have resulted from an 
      urgent need for additional personnel and resources, and were facilitated by a 
      framing of the crisis in terms of war. These deployments were in the interest of 
      armed forces and enabled them to improve their operational readiness, boost their 
      societal standing and support societies with their expertise. Even though armed 
      forces may provide crucial aid in times of need, it is important that civilian 
      crisis organizations are not undermined, civilian control and civil rights are 
      guaranteed, and the effects on other military operations are considered and 
      discussed. This Forum contribution offers some reflections and recommendations.
