TI  - Military Physicians Are Not Just Physicians in the Military: Using Leadership 
      Training in Military Graduate Medical Education to Assure Mission Success.
PG  - 61-63
LID - 10.1093/milmed/usy423 [doi]
AB  - Physicians in the military often take leadership roles much earlier in their 
      career than their civilian counterparts. Military Graduate Medical Education 
      programs must continue to provide relevant leadership training that prepares 
      graduates for their imminent leadership roles. The following article illustrates 
      the experience of a junior Army Medical Corps Officer deployed shortly after 
      residency. His case illustrates how he utilized the tools and lessons learned 
      from the professional development and leadership training in his residency to 
      assure the operational readiness and success of his unit.
