TI  - Chest pain in a young soldier.
PG  - 1237-9
AB  - Chest pain is a common complaint in the primary care setting. During the 
      evaluation of this complaint, most efforts are directed toward eliminating the 
      most serious causes of chest pain. Despite a complete evaluation, many patients 
      never receive a formal diagnosis for their complaints, which can lead to 
      frustration and continued symptoms, which can in turn affect mission readiness of 
      a unit. We report on a patient who presented to sick call during his deployment 
      with a rather unexpected finding.
